  "section": "26",
  "quote": "A landlord may enter a rental unit without written notice to clean it if the tenancy agreement requires the landlord to clean the rental unit at regular intervals and,",
  "reason": "Section 26(2) of the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 explicitly permits a landlord to enter a rental unit without written notice to clean it if the tenancy agreement requires the landlord to do so at regular intervals. Because the clause specifies entry between 10 a.m. and 2 p.m. on those days, it also satisfies the statutory requirement for agreed or permitted hours of entry."
}

